.TH XUR.STD.IO 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.io \- console I/O
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::io;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::io
provides formatted printing to stdout. Format strings use
.B {}
as placeholders, replaced by the next argument's display form.
Literal braces are written as
.B {{
and
.BR }} .
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B println(format, args...)
Print a formatted line to stdout (with trailing newline).
.TP
.B print(format, args...)
Print formatted text to stdout (no trailing newline).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::io;

fn main() {
    io::println("Hello, {}!", "world");
    io::println("{} + {} = {{}{}{}}", 1, 2, 3);
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7)
